# {{name}}

A StateSet ICP merchant — scaffolded by `@stateset/create-icp-commerce`.
Pairs [`stateset-icp-handler`](https://github.com/stateset/stateset-icp-handler)
with the embedded [iCommerce](https://github.com/stateset/stateset-icommerce)
engine in a single Rust binary.

## Run it

```bash
cargo run --release
```

First build compiles the handler (~1–2 minutes on a warm toolchain).
Subsequent `cargo run` starts in under a second.

The process serves:

- **HTTP** on `:8082` — ICP v1 + ACP / UCP / MCP compat surfaces
- **gRPC** on `:50052`
- **OpenAPI 3.1** at `GET /openapi.json`
- **Swagger UI** at `GET /docs`

## Smoke-test

```bash
curl -s http://localhost:8082/.well-known/icp \
  | jq '{tier: .conformance.tier, intents: (.intents | length)}'
```

Expected output:

```json
{ "tier": "icp-full", "intents": 17 }
```

## Buy flow from Python

```bash
pip install stateset-icp
```

```python
from stateset_icp import (
    Client, Ed25519KeyPair, create_mandate_payload, sign_mandate,
)

kp = Ed25519KeyPair.generate()
mandate = sign_mandate(
    create_mandate_payload(
        issuer=kp.did,
        subject="did:stateset:agent:demo",
        scope=["quote", "authorize", "buy"],
        budget_currency="USD",
        budget_amount_minor=50_000,
    ),
    kp,
)

with Client(
    "http://localhost:8082",
    api_key="icp_demo_key_123",
    agent_id="did:stateset:agent:demo",
) as icp:
    q = icp.quote(
        items=[{
            "sku": "WIDGET-001", "quantity": 1,
            "unit_price_hint": {"amount_minor": 2999, "currency": "USD"},
        }],
        mandate_jws=mandate,
    )
    a = icp.authorize(q["transaction"]["id"], mandate_jws=mandate)
    b = icp.buy(
        q["transaction"]["id"],
        payment={"method": "card", "token": "tok_demo",
                 "last_digits": "4242", "brand": "visa"},
        mandate_jws=mandate,
    )
    print("receipt:", b["receipt"]["jti"])
```

## Validate conformance

Once the handler is running, verify spec compliance with the reference
conformance harness:

```bash
npx @stateset/icp-conformance \
  --url http://localhost:8082 \
  --api-key icp_demo_key_123 \
  --agent-id did:stateset:agent:conformance
```

## Configure

All knobs live in `.env`. Notable defaults this scaffold wrote:

| Variable | Default | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `PORT` / `GRPC_PORT` | `8082` / `50052` | Bind ports |
| `ICP_REQUIRE_MANDATE` | `true` | Reject writes without `ICP-Mandate` |
| `ICP_VERIFY_MANDATE_SIGNATURES` | `false` | Dev-only; flip to `true` before prod |
| `ICP_ENABLE_DEMO_KEYS` | `true` | Accept `icp_demo_key_*` bearer tokens |
| `COMMERCE_DB_PATH` | `./commerce.db` | Embedded iCommerce SQLite |
| `ICP_STATE_DB_PATH` | `./icp-state.db` | Handler state (mandates, receipts) |

See [the reference handler's .env.example](https://github.com/stateset/stateset-icp-handler/blob/main/.env.example)
for the full list.

